on [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]control can reproduce get a byte-free record carrying repo, commit,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and path provenance, and every reader — CLI, Files pane, and prompt[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`@`-ref expansion — can still get their exact content on demand.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]vcs_backed_artifact_capture.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-b7[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-b7/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core: VCS-backed records and on-demand materialization[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-record[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-record: add the three VCS-provenance fields and an optional stored [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path to the artifact-file wire, admit byte-free rows, resolve them to a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]new `vcs_backed` status, and add a content-verified git materialization [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]primitive exposed through `sase_core_rs`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture policy — the authorship and version-control decision[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-policy[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-policy: add a pure decision module that classifies every capture[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]candidate as store, reference, or skip using a git probe, the repo [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inventory, the run window, and a per-run byte-copy cap, plus its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]configuration.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python record, doctor, and read 